.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt BIO_ADDRINFO 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BIO_lookup_type ,
.Nm BIO_ADDRINFO ,
.Nm BIO_ADDRINFO_next ,
.Nm BIO_ADDRINFO_free ,
.Nm BIO_ADDRINFO_family ,
.Nm BIO_ADDRINFO_socktype ,
.Nm BIO_ADDRINFO_protocol ,
.Nm BIO_ADDRINFO_address ,
.Nm BIO_lookup_ex ,
.Nm BIO_lookup
.Nd BIO_ADDRINFO type and routines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/types.h
.In openssl/bio.h
.Ft typedef union bio_addrinfo_st BIO_ADDRINFO;

 enum BIO_lookup_type {
     BIO_LOOKUP_CLIENT, BIO_LOOKUP_SERVER
 };

 int
.Fo BIO_lookup_ex
.Fa "const char *host"
.Fa "const char *service"
.Fa "int lookup_type"
.Fa "int family"
.Fa "int socktype"
.Fa "int protocol"
.Fa "BIO_ADDRINFO **res"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo BIO_lookup
.Fa "const char *host"
.Fa "const char *service"
.Fa "enum BIO_lookup_type lookup_type"
.Fa "int family"
.Fa "int socktype"
.Fa "BIO_ADDRINFO **res"
.Fc
.Ft const BIO_ADDRINFO *
.Fo BIO_ADDRINFO_next
.Fa "const BIO_ADDRINFO *bai"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo BIO_ADDRINFO_family
.Fa "const BIO_ADDRINFO *bai"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo BIO_ADDRINFO_socktype
.Fa "const BIO_ADDRINFO *bai"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo BIO_ADDRINFO_protocol
.Fa "const BIO_ADDRINFO *bai"
.Fc
.Ft const BIO_ADDR *
.Fo BIO_ADDRINFO_address
.Fa "const BIO_ADDRINFO *bai"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo BIO_ADDRINFO_free
.Fa "BIO_ADDRINFO *bai"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Vt BIO_ADDRINFO
type is a wrapper for address information types provided on your
platform.
.Pp
.Vt BIO_ADDRINFO
normally forms a chain of several that can be picked at one by one.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_lookup_ex
looks up a specified
.Fa host
and
.Fa service ,
and uses
.Fa lookup_type
to determine what the default address should be if
.Fa host
is
.Dv NULL .
.Fa family ,
.Fa socktype
and
.Fa protocol
are used to determine what protocol family, socket type and protocol
should be used for the lookup.
.Fa family
can be any of AF_INET, AF_INET6, AF_UNIX and AF_UNSPEC.
.Fa socktype
can be SOCK_STREAM, SOCK_DGRAM or 0. Specifying 0 indicates that any
type can be used.
.Fa protocol
specifies a protocol such as IPPROTO_TCP, IPPROTO_UDP or IPPORTO_SCTP.
If set to 0 than any protocol can be used.
.Fa res
points at a pointer to hold the start of a
.Vt BIO_ADDRINFO
chain.
.Pp
For the family
.Sy AF_UNIX ,
.Fn BIO_lookup_ex
will ignore the
.Fa service
parameter and expects the
.Fa host
parameter to hold the path to the socket file.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_lookup
does the same as
.Fn BIO_lookup_ex
but does not provide the ability to select based on the protocol (any
protocol may be returned).
.Pp
.Fn BIO_ADDRINFO_family
returns the family of the given
.Vt BIO_ADDRINFO .
The result will be one of the constants AF_INET, AF_INET6 and AF_UNIX.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_ADDRINFO_socktype
returns the socket type of the given
.Vt BIO_ADDRINFO .
The result will be one of the constants SOCK_STREAM and SOCK_DGRAM.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_ADDRINFO_protocol
returns the protocol id of the given
.Vt BIO_ADDRINFO .
The result will be one of the constants IPPROTO_TCP and IPPROTO_UDP.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_ADDRINFO_address
returns the underlying
.Sy BIO_ADDR
of the given
.Vt BIO_ADDRINFO .
.Pp
.Fn BIO_ADDRINFO_next
returns the next
.Vt BIO_ADDRINFO
in the chain from the given one.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_ADDRINFO_free
frees the chain of
.Vt BIO_ADDRINFO
starting with the given one.
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn BIO_lookup_ex
and
.Fn BIO_lookup
return 1 on success and 0 when an error occurred, and will leave an
error indication on the OpenSSL error stack in that case.
.Pp
All other functions described here return 0 or
.Dv NULL
when the information they should return isn't available.
.Sh NOTES
The
.Fn BIO_lookup_ex
implementation uses the platform provided
.Xr getaddrinfo 3
function.
On Linux it is known that specifying 0 for the protocol will not return
any SCTP based addresses when calling
.Xr getaddrinfo 3 .
Therefore, if an SCTP address is required then the
.Fa protocol
parameter to
.Fn BIO_lookup_ex
should be explicitly set to IPPROTO_SCTP. The same may be true on other
platforms.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn BIO_lookup_ex
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
